  "difficulty_reason": "With standard finite Coxeter geometric representation, the cyclic centralizer fact and the named noncrossing-lattice prerequisites supplied, the authors still establish source-local parabolic-projection monotonicity and folding as a noncrossing sublattice. They then propagate a moved-space reflection through its entire Coxeter-conjugation orbit to identify every noncrossing projection of an inverse Coxeter power and exclude outside preimages. This uniform reflection-geometric dynamical orbit argument across all finite irreducible Coxeter types is substantially beyond ordinary qualification-level permutation calculations.",
